## Summary

**Bug:** In `ComposeActivity.java`, the "Discard post?" / "Discard comment?" confirmation dialog registered the destructive **"Discard"** action as the *negative* button and the dismissive **"Cancel"** action as the *positive* button. Material dialogs lay buttons out right-aligned with the negative button to the *left* of the positive one, so this rendered as `[Discard] [Cancel]` — the confirming/destructive action on the left and the dismissive action on the right, which the Material guidelines explicitly call out as a "Don't" (the confirming action must be the rightmost button).

**Fix** (`app/src/main/java/com/simon/harmonichackernews/ComposeActivity.java`):

```java
.setMessage(type == TYPE_POST ? "Discard post?" : "Discard comment?")
.setNegativeButton("Cancel", null)
.setPositiveButton("Discard", new DialogInterface.OnClickListener() {
    public void onClick(DialogInterface dialog, int whichButton) {
        dialog.cancel();
        finish();
    }}).create();
```

Now the dialog renders as `[Cancel] [Discard]`, with the confirming action on the right. Behavior is otherwise unchanged: tapping Discard still cancels the dialog and finishes the activity, and Cancel simply dismisses.

**Audit of other dialogs** (per the report's request to check for the same issue):
- `ComposeActivity` formatting-info ("Dismiss"), `UserActions.showFailureDetailDialog` ("Done"), `MainActivity` changelog ("Done" + neutral "GitHub") — single-action informational dialogs; a lone button is rendered at the right edge, so ordering is already correct.
- `login_dialog.xml` — custom layout with Cancel positioned `layout_toLeftOf` Save (Save aligned to parent right): correct ordering.
- Other dialogs (`UserDialogFragment`, `CommentsSearchDialogFragment`, `DialogUtils`, comment long-press list) have no confirm/dismiss button pairs.

The discard dialog was the only offender.

